# Builder scripts

## Purpose

Build scripts produce a **distribution payload** at `DFM_DIST` (default `builder/dist/payload`). They do not install into system paths, Blender, or write `~/.dfm/setup.cfg` unless explicitly requested (`--write-local-config`).

Platform installers (DMG, tar.gz, NSIS) live under `builder/macos/`, `builder/linux/`, `builder/windows/`.

## Layout contract

```
builder/dist/payload/
├── bin/           Forester CLI + ffmpeg (+ forester.ico on Windows)
├── lib/           Native API library
├── apps/          Forester GUI (macOS .app, Linux binary, Windows .exe, optional --gui)
├── share/icons/   Forester hicolor icons (Linux)
├── addons/blender/difference_machine/
│   └── api/       Native lib + python/ bindings (embedded at build time)
├── manifest.json
├── setup.cfg.template
└── VERSION
```

Release artifacts: `builder/dist/DifferenceMachine-*`

## Script structure

- **Delegate**: `builder/build.sh` → `builder/{macos,linux,windows}/build.sh`
- **Payload path**: `builder/scripts/lib/dfm_dist.sh` — `ensure_dfm_dist`
- **Shared pipeline**: `builder/scripts/lib/build_common.sh`
- **Staging**: `builder/.staging/` — cleaned by `clean_build.sh`
- **Comments**: English only

## Avoid

- Monolithic multi-platform `build.sh` with all flags
- OS install scripts in the build pipeline
